A||||8||x-thumpr-x||Which tranny do I have?||||1||
Z||000000||x-thumpr-x||10-22-2001||11:05 PM||||help, I'm in need for a very fiero enthusiast! I'm trying to figure out which tranny is in my 85GT 4speed manual(4:10 or 3:332) If the car was drivable I could tell by the way it drives, but need to replace the throughout bearing first.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I've copied down the option codes, but need an interpreture now. What are the codes for each tranny? Or does anyone know a website that has all the option codes on it?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||10-22-2001||11:10 PM||||Don't know about tranny codes but if it's the stock tranny, it is a Muncie with 3.65 gears. Only ratio available on a '85 GT!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-23-2001||01:11 AM||||Wasn't the 4.10 jsut an option on 84SE's?<P>I love the 4.10 on my 84. I can light up the tires all the way through first, then do a nice bark into 2nd  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. This is with 16 inch wheels also!||||reg||14
Z||000003||mrfiero||10-23-2001||12:47 PM||||Here are the RPO code breakdowns for 4-sp. Fieros.<P>M19 is the 4.10 4-sp. (only available in '84)<P>MY8 is the 3.32 4-sp. (only available on '84 econo-coupes....around 6000 or so cars).<P>M17 is the 3.65 4-sp. found on '85-'86 V-6 Fieros.<P><BR>The vast majority of '84 Fieros with 4-speeds have the 4.10 ratio.......only 6000 or so "econo-coupes" were built with the 3.32 ratio.  Both were available only in 1984.<P>I hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||x-thumpr-x||10-23-2001||05:01 PM||||Thank you. Least i know know that I won't be buzzing 4000 rpm at 120km/h.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>I had a 4:10 in my 84 coupe, was good at sqwauking! Did,'t in every gear first time I drove the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> Now I got a 3:32. Lost a main bearing in the old tranny, and got very lucky with the 3:32. Thanke to the fireo shop in T.O., did a great job on the car. I was even offered $400 for the tranny a week after it was installed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||10-23-2001||08:52 PM||||Quick question, is there any possibility that my 84SE doesn't have the 4:10. I drove a different 84 with the 4:10 and it pulled a lot harder than the one I have right now....Thanks!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||x-thumpr-x||10-23-2001||08:58 PM||||A good way to tell is that a 4:10 will push close to 4000RPM's at 120km/h, while in a 3:32 you can hit 160km/h and only hit 3000RPM's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>Been there done that   LOVE IT!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>OR check the RPO codes as listed above. You'll find the ontop of the front driver side wheel. A sticker with a ****  load of 3 letter/digit codes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||10-23-2001||09:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>Quick question, is there any possibility that my 84SE doesn't have the 4:10. I drove a different 84 with the 4:10 and it pulled a lot harder than the one I have right now....Thanks!<P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not unless someone swapped out trannies......all '84 SE's got the 4.10 4-sp. (except the autos., of course).<P>Unfortunately, the M19 and MY8 look identical, so you can't tell by just looking at them.<P> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jncomutt||10-23-2001||09:51 PM||||i have an 84 with 4:10 and I can chirp em in every gear on new pavement.  It'll spin the tires from about 10mph in 3rd if its damp...  Then again, the other 84 I had could barely chirp em in 2nd and it was also 4:10, maybe because it had high miles?||||reg||1
